","type":"paragraph"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-QdiXLR":{"type":"immersive-narrative-panel","data":{"position":"start","size":"small","panelStyle":"themed"},"children":["n-YSgAps"]},"n-nxvCog":{"type":"webmap","data":{"caption":"Google Photorealistic 3D Basemap (AGSM 6.18)","map":"r-9xZ12q","timeSlider":false,"viewPlacement":"extent","extent":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"xmin":-74.01583188787433,"ymin":40.711850713008815,"xmax":-74.01070587439625,"ymax":40.71403650797575},"center":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-74.01326888113529,"y":40.712943619461825,"z":437.20773008465767},"zoom":16.128623632381853,"viewpoint":{"rotation":211.01453446435195,"scale":1584.8942975975722,"targetGeometry":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-74.01319015745077,"y":40.712844359638474,"z":430.402334228158},"camera":{"position":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-74.01584277133013,"y":40.71618875128537,"z":659.7229959219694},"heading":148.98546553564805,"tilt":62.17014264208942}},"lightingDate":1710521765000,"directShadows":false,"weather":{"type":"sunny","cloudCover":0.5},"ground":{"opacity":1},"visibleLayers":[{"id":"19353b67c58-layer-71"}],"baseMap":{"baseMapLayers":[],"groundLayers":[]},"slice":{"visible":false,"fallback":{}},"focusAreas":[]}},"n-p25Wkg":{"type":"immersive-slide","data":{"transition":"fade"},"children":["n-QdiXLR","n-nxvCog"]},"n-7hJLCg":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"...and fly onto the Brooklyn Bridge.","type":"paragraph"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-55LhbB":{"type":"immersive-narrative-panel","data":{"position":"start","size":"small","panelStyle":"themed"},"children":["n-7hJLCg"]},"n-QaDN69":{"type":"webmap","data":{"caption":"Google Photorealistic 3D Basemap (AGSM 6.18)","map":"r-zsuzmL","timeSlider":false,"viewPlacement":"extent","extent":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"xmin":-73.99687446393494,"ymin":40.70326566423378,"xmax":-73.99226329016784,"ymax":40.70523218198227},"center":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-73.99456887705139,"y":40.70424893036599,"z":35.330020879395306},"zoom":17.921330567516996,"viewpoint":{"rotation":278.39416007310047,"scale":1337.9268343860326,"targetGeometry":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-73.99473016501973,"y":40.70423089464897,"z":38.63843619823456},"camera":{"position":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":-73.9994567217,"y":40.703702252522504,"z":135.60730798356235},"heading":81.60583992689953,"tilt":76.47539920042225}},"lightingDate":1710521760000,"directShadows":false,"weather":{"type":"sunny","cloudCover":0.5},"ground":{"opacity":1},"visibleLayers":[{"id":"19353b67c58-layer-71"}],"baseMap":{"baseMapLayers":[],"groundLayers":[]},"slice":{"visible":false,"fallback":{}},"focusAreas":[],"slideSelection":"19edb1f04e8-slide-22"}},"n-EN7ir8":{"type":"immersive-slide","data":{"transition":"fade"},"children":["n-55LhbB","n-QaDN69"]},"n-9PIDvr":{"type":"immersive","data":{"type":"sidecar","subtype":"floating-panel","narrativePanelPosition":"start","narrativePanelSize":"small"},"children":["n-LiivdL","n-hnOGcM","n-RPAmP4","n-p25Wkg","n-EN7ir8"]},"n-hLFl3Y":{"type":"text","data":{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Google photorealistic basemap offers a lifelike representation of the real world, which is essential for applications such as urban planning, disaster response, and virtual tours, allowing users to create even more engaging and realistic 3D scenes, especially for urban areas and complex terrains."}},"n-uLjRVu":{"type":"separator"},"n-9Jc72Z":{"type":"text","data":{"type":"h2","text":"An immersive visualization experience","textAlignment":"center"}},"n-a0yBLy":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"The Google photorealistic basemap provides lifelike representations of more than 2,500 cities in 40 countries around the world. Behind the scenes, ArcGIS will use Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles, which will be provided as an ArcGIS-ready basemap, eliminating the previous need for specialized coding or technical skills when using the tiles directly.","type":"paragraph"}},"n-3TsVL8":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"The tiles were geared initially toward developers, and were intended for use in apps created by them. Esri has partnered with Google Maps Platform to make these dynamic photorealistic representations available to the broader GIS community. The result promises to significantly enhance the overall GIS experience. ","type":"paragraph"}},"n-CbvhGL":{"type":"text","data":{"type":"h3","text":"Take a tour of some of the world&apos;s iconic landmarks"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-uxS8bR":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"","type":"paragraph"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-dTUKZQ":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Eiffel Tower, Paris"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-ZllwI4":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Christ the Redeemer, Rio de Janeiro"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-YFQlRi":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Gateway Arch, St. Louis"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-MvyNeH":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Colosseum, Rome"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-AV285c":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Millennium Park, Chicago"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-k35xZQ":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Golden Gate Bridge, San Francisco"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-IKObZM":{"type":"action-button","data":{"text":"Walt Disney Concert Hall, Los Angeles"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-c7q6Sh":{"type":"immersive-narrative-panel","data":{"panelStyle":"themed"},"children":["n-CbvhGL","n-uxS8bR","n-dTUKZQ","n-ZllwI4","n-YFQlRi","n-MvyNeH","n-AV285c","n-k35xZQ","n-IKObZM"]},"n-D6gQ7w":{"type":"webmap","data":{"map":"r-490bd159fb3045cf95f07521f11026a4","caption":"Google Photorealistic 3D Basemap (AGSM 6.18)","timeSlider":false,"viewPlacement":"extent","extent":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"xmin":12.490113718225535,"ymin":41.88955311051142,"xmax":12.494132765466587,"ymax":41.891236215091006},"center":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":12.49212324184606,"y":41.89039466834461,"z":30.531284858472645},"zoom":17.88003888443229,"viewpoint":{"rotation":346.25599725236134,"scale":1226.5690042313768,"targetGeometry":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":12.492157603624118,"y":41.890499246179935,"z":25.14739971421659},"camera":{"position":{"spatialReference":{"wkid":4326},"x":12.491163375999744,"y":41.88747323658549,"z":180.94524933304638},"heading":13.744002747638651,"tilt":65.80607020442513}},"lightingDate":1710501002000,"directShadows":false,"weather":{"type":"sunny","cloudCover":0.5},"ground":{"opacity":0},"visibleLayers":[{"id":"19353b67c58-layer-71"}],"baseMap":{"baseMapLayers":[],"groundLayers":[]},"slice":{"visible":false,"fallback":{}},"focusAreas":[],"slideSelection":"19edb20dcd1-slide-23"}},"n-Z9Vi81":{"type":"immersive-slide","data":{"transition":"fade"},"children":["n-c7q6Sh","n-D6gQ7w"]},"n-i1Jik9":{"type":"immersive","data":{"type":"sidecar","subtype":"docked-panel","narrativePanelPosition":"start","narrativePanelSize":"small"},"children":["n-Z9Vi81"]},"n-Rq0dSo":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"","type":"paragraph"}},"n-OZRTUU":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"ArcGIS users are able to select the Google photorealistic basemap from the basemap gallery in <a href=\"https://doc.arcgis.com/en/arcgis-online/administer/configure-map.htm#ESRI_SECTION1_B98ECB95BE124A048DCD91CA03059F71\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">supported applications</a>, <a href=\"https://www.esri.com/arcgis-blog/products/arcgis-pro/announcements/bring-your-gis-to-life-with-google-photorealistic-3d-basemap\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">including ArcGIS Pro</a> and <a href=\"https://www.esri.com/arcgis-blog/products/arcgis/3d-gis/google-photorealistic-3d-basemap-now-in-preview\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ArcGIS Online Scene Viewer</a> (now in preview), Experience Builder, and Instant Apps. Users are able to create web scenes and apps, which can be shared within their organizations. The process is simple and doesn&apos;t require specialized technical skills; with just a few clicks, users are able to add the 3D basemap to their projects. ArcGIS will automatically reference the Google 3D basemap tiles, enabling a seamless and lifelike depiction of the world. ","type":"paragraph"}},"n-lm1LgH":{"type":"embed","data":{"url":"https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/c5f273648a3f442d922f14c7b9ffe194","embedType":"link","title":"Google Photorealistic Base Swipe","description":"View downtown Boston and see Google Photorealistic 3D basemap verses the Topographic 3D basemap","thumbnailUrl":"https://www.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/c5f273648a3f442d922f14c7b9ffe194/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1772736752901.png","providerUrl":"https://experience.arcgis.com","caption":"Drag the slider bar to compare the 3D basemap (left) to the Google photorealistic 3D basemap (right) in a segment of Boston waterfront.","isEmbedSupported":true,"display":"inline","embedSrc":"https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/c5f273648a3f442d922f14c7b9ffe194","allowSmallEmbeds":true,"embedResourceId":"r-OUI4t3"},"config":{"size":"wide"}},"n-nM8nRr":{"type":"separator"},"n-yaV5vO":{"type":"text","data":{"type":"h2","text":"Building your 3D foundation","textAlignment":"center"}},"n-xzspE6":{"type":"text","data":{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Google photorealistic 3D basemap serves as an excellent entry point for users diving into the 3D space who need quick access to high-resolution imagery basemap foundation. It opens the door to even more GIS users building in 3D to support and enhance their existing 2D and 3D GIS data and moving toward advanced reality mapping technology."}},"n-SaVj0m":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"For those wanting to create their own 3D basemap from imagery, <a href=\"https://www.esri.com/en-us/arcgis/products/arcgis-reality/overview\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ArcGIS Reality</a> remains the preferred solution. ArcGIS Reality is a suite of photogrammetry software products designed to enable reality capture workflows for sites, cities, and countries. Turn drone, aerial, and satellite imagery, captured either in-house or sources from a vendor, into visually stunning and highly accurate maps and 3D models. Interact with a digital world that shows places and situations as they truly are, layered with geospatial data that enriches reality with greater context.","type":"paragraph"}},"n-T77P4Y":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"Whether you need to conduct advanced urban planning, environmental assessments, or custom 3D modeling, reality mapping provides the flexibility and control necessary to meet these advanced needs, ensuring that ArcGIS continues to be the premier platform for <a href=\"https://www.esri.com/en-us/capabilities/3d-gis/features/3d-analysis\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">comprehensive 3D GIS solutions</a>.","type":"paragraph"}},"n-fC8Gn9":{"type":"separator"},"n-ZZQNTI":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"Learn more","type":"h2","textAlignment":"center"}},"n-23P33I":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"To learn more and stay informed, please read the blog article to announcement the <a href=\"https://www.esri.com/arcgis-blog/products/arcgis-online/announcements/experience-the-google-photorealistic-3d-basemap-in-arcgis-online\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Google Photorealistic 3D basemap (preview)</a> ","type":"paragraph"}},"n-X3OM82":{"type":"text","data":{"text":"You can also read this story about urban shoreline revitalization. The story utilizes the Google photorealistic 3D basemap.","type":"paragraph"}},"n-bcDtwK":{"type":"embed","data":{"url":"https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/475a49f4e93b4dabb6666fbf020fed7d","embedType":"link","title":"Waterfronts reborn","description":"Cities are transforming obsolescent shorelines into vibrant destinations. Learn about four of those urban waterfront evolutions in 3D.","thumbnailUrl":"https://cdn.arcgis.com/sharing/rest/content/items/475a49f4e93b4dabb6666fbf020fed7d/resources/wsyBvAuFyyw5fF1w09Nt3.jpg","prov